  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "National Park Hospitality Association",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to National Park Hospitality Association, the case concerns whether the Contract Disputes Act applies to contracts between the National Park Service and private concessioners."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "National Park Hospitality Association",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to National Park Hospitality Association, a regulation states that National Park Service concession contracts are not subject to the CDA, which the petitioner argues is arbitrary because some contracts are subject to the CDA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "National Park Hospitality Association",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner asserts that three contracts have been found subject to the CDA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Elwood",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 55,
              "start": 55
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Approximately 78 percent of concession contracts involve no capital improvements."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MR. ELWOOD",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Concessioners who build facilities hold a leasehold surrender interest equal to construction cost plus inflation minus depreciation, and cannot be removed until that interest is paid."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Congress",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Congress, Congress enacted the 1998 act with awareness that concessioners would build facilities, reflecting the view that concession contracts are not procurement contracts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 60,
              "start": 60
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government claims that no government funds were used in the contracts, a phrase it introduced for this case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 61,
              "start": 61
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government argues it is the sole beneficiary of contractual provisions requiring construction, repair, and maintenance of park facilities."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "14c45a11a5c2f9572bc1612451fff19287d2fd6cb53153241dd44e9c4c075b88",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-14c45a11a5c2-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 62,
              "start": 62
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court requested supplemental briefs on the issue of ripeness, due by 3:00\u202fp.m. Friday."
      }
    ],
